<title>INDIA: BSE figures of India carry forward trade - May 31.</title>
<headline>BSE figures of India carry forward trade - May 31.</headline>
<dateline>BOMBAY 1997-06-02</dateline>
<text>
<p>The following is the latest data, for the top 10 stocks by value, released by the Bombay Stock Exchange (BSE) for the carry forward or &quot;badla&quot; account ended May 31</p>
<p>.</p>
<p>SCRIP		  SETTLEMENT  AV BADLA  QTY    VALUE   % BADLA</p>
<p>			 RATE				(RS MLN)</p>
<p>----------------------------------------------------------------</p>
<p>State Bank	   305	   0.53     547700  167.05    9.06</p>
<p>Bajaj Auto	   860	   1.44	43900   37.75    8.73</p>
<p>Sterlite	     280	   0.47     131900   36.93    8.75</p>
<p>L &amp; T		  215	   0.37     162900   35.02    8.97</p>
<p>ACC		   1075	   1.81	27680   29.76    8.78</p>
<p>Castrol		430	   0.75	69150   29.73    9.09</p>
<p>MTNL		   285	   0.36	84900   24.20    6.59</p>
<p>Dr. Reddy	    215	   0.36	79000   16.99    8.73</p>
<p>BSES		   240	   0.40	65750   15.78    8.69</p>
<p>Tata Tea	     295	   0.51	47800   14.10    9.01</p>
<p>----------------------------------------------------------------</p>
<p>The average badla charges work out to 8.91 percent on an annualised basis against 10.10 percent in the previous carry forward account ended May 24.</p>
<p>-- Bombay newsroom +91-22-265 9000</p>
